 "findings": [
  "file-menu-render-bug: the File-tab click alone paints NOTHING (.se-file-menu-panel stayed display:none); the panel only renders on the next root re-render, which this census triggers with a real keystroke into the sheet (isModified flips). Viewport reads spreadsheetStore.isFileMenuOpen/activeFileMenuPanel without a mobx observer — the sheet twin of the documented word-editor File-menu bug. Every dialog pane below is censused through that side channel, one fresh page per entry, because no second re-render exists to paint a pane switch",
  "file-menu-dead-entries: 3 dialog-declaring entries reach no dialog surface (Save as...[file-menu-panel:none], Rename...[file-menu-panel:none], Version History...[menu stayed open but the entry activated no pane and no <dialog> — a dialog-declaring entry whose pane this build never renders]) — they either close the menu (non-pane action) or declare a pane the build never renders",
  "file-menu-panes-never-paint: 7 dialog panes ACTIVATE but never paint — their container is display:none (contentBoxBase in FileMenuPanel.tsx), so the pane is w=0/h=0 and no real click can reach it: Download as...→Download as, Save Copy as...→Save Copy as, Document Info...→Document Info, Access Rights...→Access Rights, Advanced Settings...→Advanced Settings, Help...→Help, Protect Document→Protect Workbook. The census enumerates each pane's shipped controls from the DOM it mounts and fires them with SYNTHETIC domDrill clicks (none portals a real <dialog>), but only the portaled ExportWizard <dialog> (1 surface painted) is actually clickable by a user",
  "file-menu-dialog-no-dismiss: Export Wizard... — the dialog's own ✕ flips activeFileMenuPanel in the store but the dialog stays open (same missing-observer re-render), so the modal cannot be closed by the user",
  "toggle-without-overlay: 6 controls flip their own active/pressed state but open nothing (left-menu/Search, left-menu/Comments, left-menu/Chat, left-menu/Spell Check, left-menu/Support, left-menu/About) — the left-menu rail has no panels in this build (.se-about-menu-panel is bound in the same non-observer Viewport as the file menu)",
  "49/59 controls open no overlay and expose no toggle state (direct-action or no-op — not decidable from the DOM): toolbar:Home/Cut, toolbar:Home/Copy, toolbar:Home/Paste, toolbar:Home/Format Painter, toolbar:Home/Bold, toolbar:Home/Italic, toolbar:Home/Underline, toolbar:Home/Strike, toolbar:Home/Increase Size, toolbar:Home/Decrease Size, toolbar:Home/Left, toolbar:Home/Center …"
 ]
}
